ntdll: recycle private unnamed semaphores without a server round trip

Unity's RenderNodeQueue creates an unnamed semaphore and closes it again on
every call of a rendering function; each NtCreateSemaphore and NtClose is a
wineserver round trip. With in-process sync (kernel or userspace ntsync),
NtCreateSemaphore of an unnamed, non-inheritable semaphore with only specific
access rights marks the handle as private (no extra server call, no fd; the
create request and the mark are made under fd_cache_mutex). Its close, if the
mark is still set and the semaphore has no other user in process, fetches its
in-process sync if it was not used in process yet (in place of the close
request), drains its count to 0 in process and parks the still-open handle in
a 64-entry free list (the oldest entry is closed for real when the list is
full). The next matching NtCreateSemaphore (same access and maximum count)
releases a parked handle to the initial count in process and returns it,
without a server call.

The mark is cleared when the handle is duplicated (by this process, or by
another process: wineserver makes another process run a duplication of a
semaphore out of this process here, as APC_DUP_HANDLE, see
server_handle_c_semaphore_recycle.patch; the unmark and the duplicate request
are made under one hold of fd_cache_mutex), has its flags or security changed,
is made permanent, is passed as a standard handle or is opened again as the
root object of NtOpenSemaphore with an empty name. A parked handle is closed
for real when one of those calls, NtQueryObject, NtCompareObjects,
NtQuerySecurityObject or NtMakeTemporaryObject reaches it, so the server
reports it as invalid.

Switch: WINE_SEMAPHORE_RECYCLE=0 disables it.

Also needs dlls_ntdll_unix_server_c_semaphore_recycle.patch,
dlls_ntdll_unix_file_c_semaphore_recycle.patch,
dlls_ntdll_unix_security_c_semaphore_recycle.patch,
dlls_ntdll_unix_process_c_semaphore_recycle.patch,
server_handle_c_semaphore_recycle.patch and
server_process_c_semaphore_recycle.patch.

